e simulator for largescale human-robot interaction launched by Meta. Based on the Bullet physics engine, Habitat has implemented highperformance, high-speed, parallel 3D simulation, and provides a rich interface for reinforcement learning of embodied agents. Habitat has extremely high degree of openness. Researchers can import and create 3D scenes in Habitat or use the rich open resources on the Habitat platform for expansion. Habitat has many customizable sensors and supports multi-agent simulation. Multiple embodied agents from open resources or customizations (e.g., humans and robot dogs) can cooperate in the simulator, move freely, and perform simple interactions with the scene. Thus, Habitat is attracting increasing attention. Different from other simulators that focus more on the scene, SAPIEN [66] pays more attention to simulate the inter
