IV. EMBODIED PERCEPTION
The “north stars” of the future of visual perception is embodied-centric visual reasoning and social intelligence [74]. Unlike merely recognizing objects in images, agent with embodied perception must move in the physical world and interact with the environment. This requires a deeper understanding of 3D space and dynamic environments. Embodied perception requires visual perception and reasoning, understanding the 3D relations within a scene, and predicting and performing complex tasks based on visual information.
